      "created_at": "2019-11-20T17:35:35Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-11-20T17:35:35Z",
      "body": "I can confirm that having the archivist name often turns out to be in DBL, for example to work out how things ended up the way they did. This works without user ids because there's only one DBL. Giving user ids may or not enable DBL to identify the user - it might well do so if the user is in the Registry. But, in all cases, it tells me that I can't assume org-x's John Smith is DBL's John Smith, and that's something.\r\n\r\nFor GDPR I'd have thought that the name of the user is more of the problem than a somewhat opaque user id (unless someone is using SS numbers as keys or something.)\r\n\r\nWe should probably make these fields optional though.",
