      "created_at": "2019-11-22T11:17:31Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-11-22T11:17:31Z",
      "body": "We added a second user identifier because the project archivist may not be the person uploading to DBL. (The total number of users who have uploaded to DBL is just over 100, with the vast majority of entries being uploaded by less than 20 users - these figures are orders of magnitude lower than the number of archivists who have prepared projects now in DBL.)\r\n\r\nI think it's good to flag GDPR but I agree that we should not make GDPR compliance a SB problem. In some cases, SBs may never be seen by anyone but the owner, in others they could potentially appear all over the place. So GDPR seems to me to be partly an ecosystem question rather than a data representation question. I would imagine that a DBL approach to this would be to extend the current \"strip on export\" mechanisms used to provide specific users with a suitable subset of information.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
